@casualjim I am new on Golang.

there is my file called as response.go

``` go
package app

import (
    "github.com/alioygur/piklook-corporate/app/domain"
    "github.com/alioygur/piklook-corporate/app/lib"
)

type times struct {
    CreatedAt int64 `json:"createdAt"`
    UpdatedAt int64 `json:"updatedAt"`
}

type response struct {
    Data interface{} `json:"data"`
}

type userRes struct {
    ID       int64  `json:"id"`
    Username string `json:"username"`
    Email    string `json:"email"`
    times
}

func newUserRes(user *domain.User) *userRes {
    res := new(userRes)
    lib.CopyTo(user, res)

    return res
}

// swagger:response jobRes
type jobRes struct {
    ID          int64       `json:"id"`
    UserID      int64       `json:"userId"`
    Title       string      `json:"title"`
    Description string      `json:"description"`
    Skills      []*skillRes `json:"skills,omitempty"`
}

type skillRes struct {
    ID   int64  `json:"id"`
    Name string `json:"name"`
}

func newJobRes(job *domain.Job) interface{} {
    res := new(jobRes)

    lib.CopyTo(job, res)

    skillRess := make([]*skillRes, len(job.Skills))

    for i, skill := range job.Skills {
        lib.CopyTo(skill, &skillRess[i])
    }

    res.Skills = skillRess

    return response{res}
}

func newJobsRes(jobs []*domain.Job) interface{} {
    res := make([]jobRes, len(jobs))
    for index, p := range jobs {
        lib.CopyTo(p, &res[index])
    }

    return response{res}
}
```

The error

``` sh
➜  piklook-corporate  swagger generate spec -o swagger.json
unknown field type ele for "skills"
```

Hey there, I'm fighting this issue and managed to track it down to an interface. I have the following interface:

``` go
// TranscodingProvider represents a provider of transcoding.
//
// It defines a basic API for transcoding a media and query the status of a
// Job. The underlying provider should handle the profileSpec as deisired (it
// might be a JSON, or an XML, or anything else.
type TranscodingProvider interface {
    JobStatus(id string) (*JobStatus, error)

    // Healthcheck should return nil if the provider is currently available
    // for transcoding videos, otherwise it should return an error
    // explaining what's going on.
    Healthcheck() error
}
```

There's no special mark-up in this interface. It considers the Healthcheck method to be an attribute. If I remove the method, it works. If I change `swaggerSchemaForType` (in go-swagger code) to treat an error as a string ([see the diff](https://gist.github.com/fsouza/fc7e6d58c6e804069dd3)), it includes TranscodingProvider as one of the definitions in the manifest, declaring it as follow:

``` json
